From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 07:43:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] packageupdate: start the placeholder in every updating task

When several applications update together, PackageUpdateController gets one
onPackageUpdateRequested() call per package and starts a PackageUpdateActivity
placeholder in the updating task of each, with the task id and avoid-move-to-front
launch options. The activity was singleTop. ActivityStarter delivers a singleTop start
to the top running activity of the focused root task when it is the same component
(deliverToCurrentTopIfNeeded), and in a desk that root task holds every freeform task:
when the topmost task is handled first, its placeholder is the desk's top activity and
the start for the next task is delivered to it as a new intent. The other task never
gets a placeholder, keeps running while its package is replaced, and is killed by the
package stop timeout without saving its state. Which package is handled first is
decided by two package update threads, so the failure comes and goes.

Make the placeholder a standard activity. Each update request names its task, so a
standard start adds exactly one placeholder to that task; a repeated request for the
same task adds a second one, which the CLEAR_TASK launch of the base intent removes
with the first. Nothing in the transition handler depends on the launch mode.

Checked on a guest by starting the placeholder as the controller does, into a desk of
two freeform tasks, topmost task first: a singleTop activity (the stock placeholder
among them) gets START_DELIVERED_TO_TOP and a new intent in the first task, and a
standard activity gets one instance in each task.
---
 libs/WindowManager/Shell/AndroidManifest.xml                | 6 ++++--
 .../wm/shell/packageupdate/PackageUpdateController.kt       | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libs/WindowManager/Shell/AndroidManifest.xml b/libs/WindowManager/Shell/AndroidManifest.xml
index 4e2bffd6dc646bf9a02bc6815d13198f865d8d3d..4da5cec4c1069e78c314f4f9b6b962909f4066a1 100644
--- a/libs/WindowManager/Shell/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/libs/WindowManager/Shell/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -40,10 +40,12 @@
             android:theme="@style/DesktopWallpaperTheme"
             android:taskAffinity="com.android.wm.shell.desktop_wallpaper"/>
 
+        <!-- A standard activity: PackageUpdateController starts one placeholder in each updating
+             task, and a singleTop placeholder is delivered as a new intent to another task's
+             placeholder when that one is the top activity of the focused root task. -->
         <activity
             android:name=".packageupdate.PackageUpdateActivity"
             android:excludeFromRecents="true"
-            android:theme="@style/PackageUpdateActivityTheme"
-            android:launchMode="singleTop" />
+            android:theme="@style/PackageUpdateActivityTheme" />
     </application>
 </manifest>
diff --git a/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/packageupdate/PackageUpdateController.kt b/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/packageupdate/PackageUpdateController.kt
index b6f4fd013b5ba5c199ed911b555a1c9efc7a09dd..4b0a88e7f81d8389514d4dd0623b657dda249519 100644
--- a/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/packageupdate/PackageUpdateController.kt
+++ b/libs/WindowManager/Shell/src/com/android/wm/shell/packageupdate/PackageUpdateController.kt
@@ -124,6 +124,9 @@ class PackageUpdateController(
         val intent =
             PackageUpdateActivity.createIntent(userContext, userId, task.taskId, icon, name)
 
+        // Each updating task gets its own placeholder. The activity is not singleTop: the activity
+        // starter delivers a singleTop start to the top activity of the focused root task, which is
+        // the placeholder of another task when that task was handled first.
         val options =
             ActivityOptions.makeBasic().apply {
                 pendingIntentBackgroundActivityStartMode =
